            // But buggy might still revert if frozen or insufficient balance?
            // We set up with enough balance and not frozen, so buggy would succeed.
            // So this test will fail on buggy version because the try block will be entered,
            // triggering the assertTrue(false), causing test failure.
            // On reference, catch block reached, no failure.
            // That meets requirement: reference passes for all inputs (non-owner burn always reverts),
            // buggy fails for some input where non-owner has balance and attempts burn.
            // So we don't need an assertTrue in catch; just doing nothing is fine (test passes).
        }
